# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your keys.
#
# The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is REQUIRED for Expo to expose a value to the app.
# Every key below is optional — with none set, Hit runs in offline "demo" mode
# using local mock data and a built-in list of 1,000+ world cities.

# --- Supabase (auth, database, realtime messaging) ----------------------
# Find these in your Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Google Places (worldwide location autocomplete) --------------------
# Without this key, location fields fall back to the offline city list.
# With it, ANY city/town/neighborhood worldwide will autocomplete.
#
# How to get a key:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick) a project.
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Places API" (and "Geocoding API").
#   3. APIs & Services → Credentials → "Create credentials" → "API key".
#   4. (Recommended) Click the key → Restrict it to the Places API, and add an
#      application restriction for your app's bundle id / package name.
#   5. Make sure billing is enabled on the project (Google requires it; there
#      is a generous monthly free tier for Places autocomplete).
#   6. Paste the key on the line below, then restart Expo with: npx expo start -c
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
